[[Kankadadka]] is the {{w|capital city|capital}} of [[Burawa]]. The city is wholely inside of the city of [[Samara]] excluding it's eastern border of the [[Qaybin river]]. The city was named after the village it replaced. Kankadadka is a {{w|planned city|planned city}}, established by the [[Capital City Act of 1932]] as part of political reforms during the [[Socialist transition of Burawa]] era. 

Kankadadka was built as a model city of egalitarianism set by the architect [[Jalil Francois]], where all structures facades would match each other, but interiors would be vastly different. The city would be 8km by 8km wide, with an area of 64km. The location was chosen due to it's proximity to the former capital city, [[Samara]]. The city's construction commenced in 1935, but was paused due to the [[Great Adonian War]]. The city restarted construction in 1956 and officially completed it's last structure in 1973.

The city acts as home of the [[Parliament of Burawa]], the [[Leader of the Burawi People]] and many major government institutions. Kankadadka main industries are government, education and tourism, with over 7 million tourists a year, the third most popular city to visit in the country.